<title>INDIA: India's SBI Commercial &amp; Intl cuts PLR to 15.5 pct.</title>
<headline>India's SBI Commercial &amp; Intl cuts PLR to 15.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>SBI Commercial &amp; International Bank Ltd said on Tuesday it will cut its prime lending rate to 15.5 percent per annum from 16.5 percent from May 1.</p>
<p>The revised rate is exclusive of interest tax, a bank official told Reuters.</p>
<p>The rate cut follows measures announced by the Reserve Bank of India to reduce deposit rates in its monetary policy for first half 1997/98 (April-March) released on April 15.</p>
<p>The official said the bank's deposit rates effective May 1 are as follows:</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>Maturity			   Interest (percent per annum)</p>
<p>-----------------		----------------------------</p>
<p>30-89 days				   8.0</p>
<p>90-1 year				    9.0</p>
<p>Above 1 year to 2 year		  12.0</p>
<p>Above 2 years to 5 years		13.0</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>	  The official said the bank's non-resident external (NRE)</p>
<p>and non-resident non-repatriable (NRNR) deposit rates effective May 1 are as follows:</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>Maturity			   Interest (percent per annum)</p>
<p>-----------------		----------------------------</p>
<p>6 months - 1 year			  9.0</p>
<p>Above 1 year to 2 years		 12.0</p>
<p>Above 2 year to 3 years		 13.0</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
